{
  "id": 325803819,
  "iid": 17200,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: use units for relative time labels",
  "description": "For label strings, display FT_RELATIVE_TIME fields using strings\nwith presumably human-friendly notation, showing sub-second times\nas \"milliseconds,\" \"microseconds\", or \"nanoseconds\", and showing\nlarger times like \"n hours, m minutes, s.s seconds,\" instead of\njust appending \"seconds\" to a floating point number of seconds.\n\nThis only affects the label as used in the protocol tree. In other\ncases where the string representing a FT_RELATIVE_TIME was a\nfloating point number representing seconds with no unit suffix,\nkeep it as such; e.g. filtering, generating a filter to apply,\nwriting to JSON or PDML. For the same reason, do not change the\n\"display label\" (from proto_item_fill_display_label) that is used\nfor custom columns and packet diagrams nor the string returned from\nproto_tree_add_item_ret_time_string().\n\nMake this the default for all fields. Some fields, or some users,\nmight prefer continuing to use floating point seconds exclusively.\nWe could, as noted, add a display format option for certain fields,\nor a preference that users could set. There already is a preference\nvalue for displaying the \"generic timestamp column\" using days,\nminutes, and seconds; that could perhaps be re-used (or not, as\na user might want relative times one way but the timestamp column\na different way.)\n\nFix #11727",
